From 508ac554a94c4aea8b4a62a1b9a7b0cb85fb0c16 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 03:06:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(routing): Part G — single-host tenant routing; kill NXDOMAIN subdomains

No wildcard DNS exists for *.vowos.bridgebox.ai or *.bridgebox.ai (verified
2026-08-20: every {slug} host is NXDOMAIN). Login, the workspace selector and
the onboarding wizard all built tenant URLs from a slug, so every organization
created in the wizard dead-ended on DNS_PROBE_FINISHED_NXDOMAIN.

- Route real tenants to same-origin /workspace. NOT /app, which server.js
  302s to the /demoapp sandbox on the marketing host.
- Drop the central-auth token hand-off on these paths; the session already
  belongs to this origin.
- Persist the chosen organization (localStorage) so multi-workspace users keep
  the disambiguation the hostname used to provide.
- Split the AuthContext bootstrap query: one 400 on a nested embed was setting
  tenant=null and rendering the entire workspace blank.
- Add a mutation-verified guard test that fails if any source file builds a
  hostname from a slug.
